     "id": "37bec5ece5ab4c8fc6ac33359677136d964e93ae",
     "tree_id": "5025da47d4d5b26698abc2752431d82846af00b1",
     "message": "Pin the pagination flags the run lookup depends on\n\nDropping --paginate --slurp from the workflow-run lookup left both\npackages green. routedRunner routed on \"actions/runs\" and ignored every\nother argument, so the advertised argv was never checked.\n\nThe flags are part of the API contract rather than a detail. Without\n--paginate the endpoint answers with a single {\"workflow_runs\":[...]}\nobject instead of an array of pages, so the decode fails, cancelledRuns\ngoes nil, and every gate skipped by a cancelled dependency quietly\nreturns to publishing failure. The degradation is fail-closed, which is\nwhy nothing else noticed it.\n\nFound by the round-2 review of this branch as its one surviving\nmutation. Refs #6189",
     "timestamp": "2026-08-23T13:58:33Z",
